IMPORT prelude
IMPORT `topca-minor`

-- Tobacco and Other Products Control Act 2006 (WA) -- the Q&A layer: the questions people ask, with the seat and the
-- situation as parameters.
--
-- PURPOSE. One module whose exported questions serve every seat from one deployment. Every exported question takes
-- `my role` first ("Which of these describes you"). A question about another role answers `does not arise for you`
-- without reading any other input, so the site's question form never asks those inputs and drops the question.
--
-- ROLES. The baseline (topca-minor.l4) was written from the seat of a person under 18 with, or wanting, tobacco or a
-- vape. Two more people meet the Act's sale and supply rules:
--   - the young person under 18: every baseline question;
--   - the seller or supplier of tobacco products, smoking implements or vapes (ss 6, 12, 13, 15(1), 30A, 106);
--   - a parent or other adult dealing with someone under 18 who is asked to buy, give or pass on tobacco or a vape for
--     them (ss 6, 7, 30A, "supply" in the Glossary), or who is told of a finding (s 101).
-- Investigators and police officers are never seats: what they may do (seize, use force, ask for details, tell a
-- parent) appears as what it means for the person asking.
--
-- SITUATIONS (design D8 of the Graffiti Vandalism Act encoding). Within a role, a question that arises only in a
-- situation takes that situation's fact straight after `my role`, and answers `does not arise for you` when it does not
-- hold, without reading anything else. The questions of one situation share one input (same name, type and @desc).
--   - `someone sold or supplied the item to me` (BOOLEAN): the young person's questions of the sale or supply to them
--     (ss 6, 30A, 106, 13, and the seller's s 6 fine). FALSE: does not arise.
--   - `who found the young person` (`Who found me`): ss 99(1)-(3), 100, 101, for the young person, and s 101 for the
--     adult. `someone else`: does not arise (only an investigator or a police officer has those powers, s 79(1)).
--   - `the item was taken from me` (BOOLEAN): s 99(4), (5), what happens to it. FALSE: does not arise.
--   - `I am said to have sold or supplied tobacco to someone under 18` (BOOLEAN): the seller's s 13 defence. FALSE: does
--     not arise.
-- A question that arises in every situation of its role takes no situation input.
--
-- The rules are in topca-minor.l4. This module calls them and restates none; for the young person each answer is the
-- baseline export's own answer, wrapped. The seller's and the adult's sale and supply question builds the baseline's
-- `My item` from the person it goes to, through a helper. No exported question takes a DEONTIC or EVENT input.
--
-- BASELINE. Not for public use as advice. See NOTES.md, "Q&A layer (seat and situations as parameters)".

§ `Tobacco and Other Products Control Act 2006 (WA) -- the questions people ask`

§§ `Who is asking, and the shape of the answers`

DECLARE Role IS ONE OF
    `I am under 18, and have or want tobacco, a smoking implement or a vape`
    `I sell or supply tobacco products, smoking implements or vapes`
    `I am a parent or other adult asked to buy, give or pass on tobacco or a vape for someone under 18`

DECLARE `Yes or no` IS ONE OF
    yes
    no
    `does not arise for you`

DECLARE `Amount` IS ONE OF
    `does not arise for you`
    amount HAS dollars IS A NUMBER

DECLARE `My possession, if it arises` IS ONE OF
    `does not arise for you`
    `the answer is` HAS `the answer` IS A `What my possession is`

DECLARE `The sale or supply, if it arises` IS ONE OF
    `does not arise for you`
    `the answer is` HAS `the answer` IS A `What the supply to me is`

DECLARE `My seized item, if it arises` IS ONE OF
    `does not arise for you`
    `the answer is` HAS `the answer` IS A `What happens to my seized item`

DECLARE `Words` IS ONE OF
    `does not arise for you`
    `the answer is` HAS `the answer` IS A STRING

§§ `Helpers`

GIVEN `it holds` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A `Yes or no`
`yes if` `it holds` MEANS
    IF `it holds` THEN yes ELSE no

-- The baseline's `My item` for an item sold or supplied to someone: what it is, the day, the age of the person it goes
-- to, and the s 30A(3) conditions. The quantities are read only by the possession questions, which do not use this, so
-- they are 0.
GIVEN `what it is` IS A `Kind of item`
      `the day` IS A DATE
      `their age` IS A NUMBER
      `the conditions are met` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A `My item`
`the item as supplied to someone aged` `what it is` `the day` `their age` `the conditions are met` MEANS
    `My item` WITH
        `what it is` IS `what it is`
        `the day` IS `the day`
        `my age in years` IS `their age`
        `how much I hold` IS 0
        `the personal use quantity for that kind` IS 0
        `the commercial quantity for that kind` IS 0
        `the large commercial quantity for that kind` IS 0
        `the prescribed therapeutic conditions are met` IS `the conditions are met`

-- The baseline's answer to "Would an adult who buys this item for me offend" speaks as the young person in one of its
-- four answers ("s 30A, by supplying it to me"); for the adult asking, that answer names the young person instead.
GIVEN `the answer` IS A STRING
GIVETH A STRING
`in the adult's words` `the answer` MEANS
    IF `the answer` EQUALS "s 30A, by supplying it to me"
    THEN "s 30A, by supplying it to the young person"
    ELSE `the answer`

§§ `For everyone`

§§§ `The edition, and what the item is`

@export Does the deposited edition of the Act answer for this day, on or after 13 May 2026 (Tobacco and Other Products Control Act 2006 (WA), as amended by No. 1 of 2026)?
GIVEN `my role` IS A Role @desc Which of these describes you
      `the day asked about` IS A DATE @desc The day of the event you are asking about, ISO 8601
GIVETH A `Yes or no`
`Does the deposited edition answer for the day I ask about` MEANS
    CONSIDER `my role`
    WHEN `I am under 18, and have or want tobacco, a smoking implement or a vape` THEN `yes if` (`Does the deposited edition answer for` `the day asked about`)
    WHEN `I sell or supply tobacco products, smoking implements or vapes` THEN `yes if` (`Does the deposited edition answer for` `the day asked about`)
    WHEN `I am a parent or other adult asked to buy, give or pass on tobacco or a vape for someone under 18` THEN `yes if` (`Does the deposited edition answer for` `the day asked about`)

@export Is this item a prohibited product under the Act (Tobacco and Other Products Control Act 2006 (WA) Glossary, "prohibited product")?
GIVEN `my role` IS A Role @desc Which of these describes you
      `the item` IS A `Kind of item` @desc What the item is
GIVETH A `Yes or no`
`Is this item a prohibited product` MEANS
    CONSIDER `my role`
    WHEN `I am under 18, and have or want tobacco, a smoking implement or a vape` THEN `yes if` (`Is it a prohibited product` `the item`)
    WHEN `I sell or supply tobacco products, smoking implements or vapes` THEN `yes if` (`Is it a prohibited product` `the item`)
    WHEN `I am a parent or other adult asked to buy, give or pass on tobacco or a vape for someone under 18` THEN `yes if` (`Is it a prohibited product` `the item`)

§§ `For the young person under 18`

§§§ `s 30B -- is my possession an offence`

@export Is my possession of this item an offence under the Act, and which (Tobacco and Other Products Control Act 2006 (WA) s 30B)?
GIVEN `my role` IS A Role @desc Which of these describes you
      `my item` IS A `My item` @desc The item and the facts about it
GIVETH A `My possession, if it arises`
`Is my possession of this item an offence` MEANS
    CONSIDER `my role`
    WHEN `I am under 18, and have or want tobacco, a smoking implement or a vape` THEN `the answer is` (`Is my possession an offence` `my item`)
    OTHERWISE `does not arise for you`

@export What is the most I can be fined for my possession, in dollars (first offence, on indictment) (Tobacco and Other Products Control Act 2006 (WA) s 30B(2), (4), (5); Glossary, tier 4 penalty)?
GIVEN `my role` IS A Role @desc Which of these describes you
      `my item` IS A `My item` @desc The item and the facts about it
GIVETH AN `Amount`
`What is the most I can be fined for possessing this item` MEANS
    CONSIDER `my role`
    WHEN `I am under 18, and have or want tobacco, a smoking implement or a vape` THEN amount (`What is the most I can be fined for my possession` `my item`)
    OTHERWISE `does not arise for you`

§§§ `ss 6, 13, 30A, 106 -- the sale or supply to me`

@export Was selling or supplying this item to me an offence under the Act, and which (Tobacco and Other Products Control Act 2006 (WA) ss 6, 30A)?
GIVEN `my role` IS A Role @desc Which of these describes you
      `someone sold or supplied the item to me` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Whether someone sold, gave, provided or offered the item to you (a friend handing it over supplies it, Glossary "supply")
      `my item` IS A `My item` @desc The item and the facts about it
GIVETH A `The sale or supply, if it arises`
`Was selling or supplying this item to me an offence` MEANS
    CONSIDER `my role`
    WHEN `I am under 18, and have or want tobacco, a smoking implement or a vape` THEN
        IF `someone sold or supplied the item to me`
        THEN `the answer is` (`Was the supply to me an offence` `my item`)
        ELSE `does not arise for you`
    OTHERWISE `does not arise for you`

@export Was selling me this item an offence under s 106, as a look-alike of tobacco or a vape (Tobacco and Other Products Control Act 2006 (WA) s 106)?
GIVEN `my role` IS A Role @desc Which of these describes you
      `someone sold or supplied the item to me` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Whether someone sold, gave, provided or offered the item to you (a friend handing it over supplies it, Glossary "supply")
      `the item` IS A `Kind of item` @desc What the item is
GIVETH A `Yes or no`
`Was selling me this look-alike an offence` MEANS
    CONSIDER `my role`
    WHEN `I am under 18, and have or want tobacco, a smoking implement or a vape` THEN
        IF `someone sold or supplied the item to me`
        THEN `yes if` (`Was selling me a look-alike an offence` `the item`)
        ELSE `does not arise for you`
    OTHERWISE `does not arise for you`

@export What is the most the seller can be fined for selling tobacco to me under s 6, in dollars (Tobacco and Other Products Control Act 2006 (WA) s 6; Glossary, tier 1 penalty)?
GIVEN `my role` IS A Role @desc Which of these describes you
      `someone sold or supplied the item to me` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Whether someone sold, gave, provided or offered the item to you (a friend handing it over supplies it, Glossary "supply")
      `the seller is a body corporate` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Whether the seller is a company
      `it is the seller's second or later offence` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Whether the seller has offended before
GIVETH AN `Amount`
`What is the most the seller who sold to me can be fined under s 6` MEANS
    CONSIDER `my role`
    WHEN `I am under 18, and have or want tobacco, a smoking implement or a vape` THEN
        IF `someone sold or supplied the item to me`
        THEN amount (`What is the most the seller can be fined under s 6` `the seller is a body corporate` `it is the seller's second or later offence`)
        ELSE `does not arise for you`
    OTHERWISE `does not arise for you`

@export Does the seller who sold me tobacco have the s 13 defence (Tobacco and Other Products Control Act 2006 (WA) s 13(2))?
GIVEN `my role` IS A Role @desc Which of these describes you
      `someone sold or supplied the item to me` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Whether someone sold, gave, provided or offered the item to you (a friend handing it over supplies it, Glossary "supply")
      `the seller had no reason to believe I was under 18` IS A BOOLEAN @desc As the court would find it
      `my age in years` IS A NUMBER @desc Your age in years at the time
      `I produced evidence that I was 18` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Whether you showed a s 15(1) document saying you were 18
      `the s 25 warning signs were displayed` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Whether the required warning signs were up
GIVETH A `Yes or no`
`Does the seller who sold me tobacco have the s 13 defence` MEANS
    CONSIDER `my role`
    WHEN `I am under 18, and have or want tobacco, a smoking implement or a vape` THEN
        IF `someone sold or supplied the item to me`
        THEN `yes if` (`Does the seller have the s 13 defence` `the seller had no reason to believe I was under 18` `my age in years` `I produced evidence that I was 18` `the s 25 warning signs were displayed`)
        ELSE `does not arise for you`
    OTHERWISE `does not arise for you`

§§§ `ss 7, 12, 15 -- getting it, and proof of age`

@export Would I commit an offence in getting this item, by using someone else's or a forged ID (Tobacco and Other Products Control Act 2006 (WA) s 15(2))?
GIVEN `my role` IS A Role @desc Which of these describes you
      `the item` IS A `Kind of item` @desc What the item is
      `I used another person's ID` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Whether you used someone else's identification
      `I used a forged or tampered ID` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Whether you used a forged or altered identification
GIVETH A `Yes or no`
`Would I commit an offence in getting this item` MEANS
    CONSIDER `my role`
    WHEN `I am under 18, and have or want tobacco, a smoking implement or a vape` THEN `yes if` (`Would I offend in getting it` `the item` `I used another person's ID` `I used a forged or tampered ID`)
    OTHERWISE `does not arise for you`

@export Would an adult who buys this item for me commit an offence, and which (Tobacco and Other Products Control Act 2006 (WA) ss 7, 30A)?
GIVEN `my role` IS A Role @desc Which of these describes you
      `the item` IS A `Kind of item` @desc What the item is
      `my age in years` IS A NUMBER @desc Your age in years at the time
GIVETH A `Words`
`Would an adult who buys this item for me offend` MEANS
    CONSIDER `my role`
    WHEN `I am under 18, and have or want tobacco, a smoking implement or a vape` THEN `the answer is` (`Would an adult buying it for me offend` `the item` `my age in years`)
    OTHERWISE `does not arise for you`

@export Is this document proof that I have reached 18 (Tobacco and Other Products Control Act 2006 (WA) s 15(1))?
GIVEN `my role` IS A Role @desc Which of these describes you
      `the document` IS A `Kind of document` @desc The document shown
      `it has my photograph` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Whether it bears your photograph
      `it shows I am 18 or over` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Whether it shows, by date of birth or otherwise, that you have reached 18
GIVETH A `Yes or no`
`Is this document proof that I have reached 18` MEANS
    CONSIDER `my role`
    WHEN `I am under 18, and have or want tobacco, a smoking implement or a vape` THEN `yes if` (`Is this document proof of my age` `the document` `it has my photograph` `it shows I am 18 or over`)
    OTHERWISE `does not arise for you`

@export May the seller refuse to sell me this item unless I prove I am 18 (Tobacco and Other Products Control Act 2006 (WA) s 12)?
GIVEN `my role` IS A Role @desc Which of these describes you
      `the item` IS A `Kind of item` @desc What the item is
GIVETH A `Yes or no`
`May the seller refuse to sell me this item without proof of age` MEANS
    CONSIDER `my role`
    WHEN `I am under 18, and have or want tobacco, a smoking implement or a vape` THEN `yes if` (`May the seller refuse me without proof of age` `the item`)
    OTHERWISE `does not arise for you`

§§§ `ss 98-101 -- what may be done to me, and to what is found on me`

@export May the item be taken from me (Tobacco and Other Products Control Act 2006 (WA) s 99(1)-(3))?
GIVEN `my role` IS A Role @desc Which of these describes you
      `who found the young person` IS A `Who found me` @desc Who found the person under 18 (you, or the young person you are asking about) smoking, vaping, with the item or trying to get it
      `the item` IS A `Kind of item` @desc What the item is
      `they suspect on reasonable grounds I am under 18` IS A BOOLEAN @desc As the officer would say
      `I was asked for a s 15(1) document` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Whether you were asked for a passport, licence or prescribed document
      `I produced one showing I am 18` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Whether you showed such a document then and there
GIVETH A `Yes or no`
`May the item be taken from me by an investigator or police officer` MEANS
    CONSIDER `my role`
    WHEN `I am under 18, and have or want tobacco, a smoking implement or a vape` THEN
        IF (`who found the young person` EQUALS `an investigator` OR `who found the young person` EQUALS `a police officer`)
        THEN `yes if` (`May the item be taken from me` `the item` `who found the young person` `they suspect on reasonable grounds I am under 18` `I was asked for a s 15(1) document` `I produced one showing I am 18`)
        ELSE `does not arise for you`
    OTHERWISE `does not arise for you`

@export May force be used to take the item from me (Tobacco and Other Products Control Act 2006 (WA) s 99(2))?
GIVEN `my role` IS A Role @desc Which of these describes you
      `who found the young person` IS A `Who found me` @desc Who found the person under 18 (you, or the young person you are asking about) smoking, vaping, with the item or trying to get it
GIVETH A `Yes or no`
`May force be used to take the item from me` MEANS
    CONSIDER `my role`
    WHEN `I am under 18, and have or want tobacco, a smoking implement or a vape` THEN
        IF (`who found the young person` EQUALS `an investigator` OR `who found the young person` EQUALS `a police officer`)
        THEN `yes if` (`May force be used to take it` `who found the young person`)
        ELSE `does not arise for you`
    OTHERWISE `does not arise for you`

@export What happens to my item after it is taken (Tobacco and Other Products Control Act 2006 (WA) s 99(4), (5))?
GIVEN `my role` IS A Role @desc Which of these describes you
      `the item was taken from me` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Whether an investigator or a police officer has seized the item from you under s 99
      `the item` IS A `Kind of item` @desc What the item is
      `days after seizure I produced proof I was 18` IS A NUMBER @desc Days after the seizure you showed a s 15(1) document; a large number if never
      `the proof shows I was 18 when it was taken` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Whether that document shows you had reached 18 at the seizure
GIVETH A `My seized item, if it arises`
`What happens to my item after it is taken` MEANS
    CONSIDER `my role`
    WHEN `I am under 18, and have or want tobacco, a smoking implement or a vape` THEN
        IF `the item was taken from me`
        THEN `the answer is` (`What happens to my seized item` `the item` `days after seizure I produced proof I was 18` `the proof shows I was 18 when it was taken`)
        ELSE `does not arise for you`
    OTHERWISE `does not arise for you`

@export Must I give my name and address, my parent's, and who supplied me, when asked (Tobacco and Other Products Control Act 2006 (WA) s 100)?
GIVEN `my role` IS A Role @desc Which of these describes you
      `who found the young person` IS A `Who found me` @desc Who found the person under 18 (you, or the young person you are asking about) smoking, vaping, with the item or trying to get it
      `I was smoking or vaping or had the item` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Whether you were found smoking, vaping or in possession
      `my age in years` IS A NUMBER @desc Your age in years at the time
GIVETH A `Yes or no`
`Must I give my details when asked` MEANS
    CONSIDER `my role`
    WHEN `I am under 18, and have or want tobacco, a smoking implement or a vape` THEN
        IF (`who found the young person` EQUALS `an investigator` OR `who found the young person` EQUALS `a police officer`)
        THEN `yes if` (`Must I give my details` `who found the young person` `I was smoking or vaping or had the item` `my age in years`)
        ELSE `does not arise for you`
    OTHERWISE `does not arise for you`

@export What is the most I can be fined for refusing or lying under s 100, in dollars (Tobacco and Other Products Control Act 2006 (WA) s 100(2))?
GIVEN `my role` IS A Role @desc Which of these describes you
      `who found the young person` IS A `Who found me` @desc Who found the person under 18 (you, or the young person you are asking about) smoking, vaping, with the item or trying to get it
      `I was smoking or vaping or had the item` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Whether you were found smoking, vaping or in possession
      `my age in years` IS A NUMBER @desc Your age in years at the time
GIVETH AN `Amount`
`What is the most I can be fined for refusing or lying when asked` MEANS
    CONSIDER `my role`
    WHEN `I am under 18, and have or want tobacco, a smoking implement or a vape` THEN
        IF (`who found the young person` EQUALS `an investigator` OR `who found the young person` EQUALS `a police officer`)
        THEN amount (`What is the most I can be fined under s 100` `who found the young person` `I was smoking or vaping or had the item` `my age in years`)
        ELSE `does not arise for you`
    OTHERWISE `does not arise for you`

§§ `For the young person, and for a parent or other adult`

§§§ `s 101 -- telling a parent`

@export May a parent be told that the young person was found smoking, vaping, with the item or trying to get it (Tobacco and Other Products Control Act 2006 (WA) s 101)?
GIVEN `my role` IS A Role @desc Which of these describes you
      `who found the young person` IS A `Who found me` @desc Who found the person under 18 (you, or the young person you are asking about) smoking, vaping, with the item or trying to get it
      `the young person was smoking, vaping, had the item or was trying to get it` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Whether the person under 18 (you, or the young person) was found smoking, vaping, with the item, or trying to get it
GIVETH A `Yes or no`
`May a parent be told of the finding` MEANS
    CONSIDER `my role`
    WHEN `I am under 18, and have or want tobacco, a smoking implement or a vape` THEN
        IF (`who found the young person` EQUALS `an investigator` OR `who found the young person` EQUALS `a police officer`)
        THEN `yes if` (`May my parent be told` `who found the young person` `the young person was smoking, vaping, had the item or was trying to get it`)
        ELSE `does not arise for you`
    WHEN `I am a parent or other adult asked to buy, give or pass on tobacco or a vape for someone under 18` THEN
        IF (`who found the young person` EQUALS `an investigator` OR `who found the young person` EQUALS `a police officer`)
        THEN `yes if` (`May my parent be told` `who found the young person` `the young person was smoking, vaping, had the item or was trying to get it`)
        ELSE `does not arise for you`
    OTHERWISE `does not arise for you`

§§ `For the seller or supplier, and for a parent or other adult`

§§§ `ss 6, 30A -- selling or supplying to this person`

-- s 6: "A person must not sell, supply or deliver a tobacco product or a tobacco smoking implement to a person who has
-- not reached 18 years of age." s 30A(1): "A person who sells or supplies a prohibited product commits a crime", to
-- anyone; (3): not a therapeutic vaping product on the prescribed conditions. Glossary: "supply includes to provide, or
-- offer to provide, whether or not gratuitously" -- so a parent who hands their child a cigarette supplies it. The
-- baseline's rule, run over the item as supplied to that person.
@export Would it be an offence for me to sell, give or supply this item to this person, and which (Tobacco and Other Products Control Act 2006 (WA) ss 6, 30A; Glossary, "supply")?
GIVEN `my role` IS A Role @desc Which of these describes you
      `the item` IS A `Kind of item` @desc What the item is
      `the day of the sale or supply` IS A DATE @desc The day of the sale or supply, ISO 8601
      `the age in years of the person it goes to` IS A NUMBER @desc The age in years of the person you sell, give or supply it to
      `the sale or supply meets the prescribed therapeutic conditions` IS A BOOLEAN @desc For a therapeutic vaping product: whether the sale or supply meets the conditions the regulations prescribe (s 30A(3)); otherwise false
GIVETH A `The sale or supply, if it arises`
`Would it be an offence for me to sell or supply this item to this person` MEANS
    CONSIDER `my role`
    WHEN `I sell or supply tobacco products, smoking implements or vapes` THEN `the answer is` (`Was the supply to me an offence` (`the item as supplied to someone aged` `the item` `the day of the sale or supply` `the age in years of the person it goes to` `the sale or supply meets the prescribed therapeutic conditions`))
    WHEN `I am a parent or other adult asked to buy, give or pass on tobacco or a vape for someone under 18` THEN `the answer is` (`Was the supply to me an offence` (`the item as supplied to someone aged` `the item` `the day of the sale or supply` `the age in years of the person it goes to` `the sale or supply meets the prescribed therapeutic conditions`))
    OTHERWISE `does not arise for you`

§§ `For the seller or supplier`

§§§ `ss 6, 106 -- the penalties for selling`

@export What is the most I can be fined for selling or supplying tobacco to someone under 18, in dollars (Tobacco and Other Products Control Act 2006 (WA) s 6; Glossary, tier 1 penalty)?
GIVEN `my role` IS A Role @desc Which of these describes you
      `I am a body corporate` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Whether you sell as a company
      `it would be my second or later offence` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Whether you have been convicted of an offence before
GIVETH AN `Amount`
`What is the most I can be fined for selling tobacco to someone under 18` MEANS
    CONSIDER `my role`
    WHEN `I sell or supply tobacco products, smoking implements or vapes` THEN amount (`What is the most the seller can be fined under s 6` `I am a body corporate` `it would be my second or later offence`)
    OTHERWISE `does not arise for you`

@export Is it an offence for me to sell this item as a look-alike of tobacco or a vape (Tobacco and Other Products Control Act 2006 (WA) s 106)?
GIVEN `my role` IS A Role @desc Which of these describes you
      `the item` IS A `Kind of item` @desc What the item is
GIVETH A `Yes or no`
`Is it an offence for me to sell this look-alike` MEANS
    CONSIDER `my role`
    WHEN `I sell or supply tobacco products, smoking implements or vapes` THEN `yes if` (`Was selling me a look-alike an offence` `the item`)
    OTHERWISE `does not arise for you`

§§§ `ss 12, 13, 15(1) -- proof of age`

@export May I refuse to sell this item unless the buyer proves they are 18 (Tobacco and Other Products Control Act 2006 (WA) s 12)?
GIVEN `my role` IS A Role @desc Which of these describes you
      `the item` IS A `Kind of item` @desc What the item is
GIVETH A `Yes or no`
`May I refuse to sell this item without proof of age` MEANS
    CONSIDER `my role`
    WHEN `I sell or supply tobacco products, smoking implements or vapes` THEN `yes if` (`May the seller refuse me without proof of age` `the item`)
    OTHERWISE `does not arise for you`

@export Is this document the buyer shows me proof that they have reached 18 (Tobacco and Other Products Control Act 2006 (WA) s 15(1))?
GIVEN `my role` IS A Role @desc Which of these describes you
      `the document` IS A `Kind of document` @desc The document shown
      `it has the buyer's photograph` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Whether it bears the buyer's photograph
      `it shows the buyer is 18 or over` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Whether it shows, by date of birth or otherwise, that the buyer has reached 18
GIVETH A `Yes or no`
`Is this document proof that the buyer has reached 18` MEANS
    CONSIDER `my role`
    WHEN `I sell or supply tobacco products, smoking implements or vapes` THEN `yes if` (`Is this document proof of my age` `the document` `it has the buyer's photograph` `it shows the buyer is 18 or over`)
    OTHERWISE `does not arise for you`

-- s 13(2): the defence to s 6 (and ss 7, 8(1), 9), from the seller's side; the baseline's rule with the buyer's facts.
@export Do I have the s 13 defence to selling or supplying tobacco to someone under 18 (Tobacco and Other Products Control Act 2006 (WA) s 13(2))?
GIVEN `my role` IS A Role @desc Which of these describes you
      `I am said to have sold or supplied tobacco to someone under 18` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Whether you are said (for example, charged) to have sold, supplied or delivered a tobacco product or smoking implement to a person under 18 (s 6)
      `I had no reason to believe the buyer was under 18` IS A BOOLEAN @desc As the court would find it
      `the buyer's age in years` IS A NUMBER @desc The buyer's age in years at the time
      `the buyer produced evidence of being 18` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Whether the buyer showed a s 15(1) document saying they were 18, at or before the sale
      `the s 25 warning signs were displayed` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Whether the required warning signs were up
GIVETH A `Yes or no`
`Do I have the s 13 defence` MEANS
    CONSIDER `my role`
    WHEN `I sell or supply tobacco products, smoking implements or vapes` THEN
        IF `I am said to have sold or supplied tobacco to someone under 18`
        THEN `yes if` (`Does the seller have the s 13 defence` `I had no reason to believe the buyer was under 18` `the buyer's age in years` `the buyer produced evidence of being 18` `the s 25 warning signs were displayed`)
        ELSE `does not arise for you`
    OTHERWISE `does not arise for you`

§§ `For a parent or other adult`

§§§ `ss 7, 30A -- buying it for them`

-- s 7: "A person must not purchase a tobacco product or a tobacco smoking implement on behalf of a person who has not
-- reached 18 years of age"; for a vape, handing it on is a supply (s 30A). The baseline's rule, asked about the young
-- person.
@export Would I commit an offence by buying this item for the young person, and which (Tobacco and Other Products Control Act 2006 (WA) ss 7, 30A)?
GIVEN `my role` IS A Role @desc Which of these describes you
      `the item` IS A `Kind of item` @desc What the item is
      `the young person's age in years` IS A NUMBER @desc The age in years of the person you would buy it for
GIVETH A `Words`
`Would I commit an offence by buying this item for the young person` MEANS
    CONSIDER `my role`
    WHEN `I am a parent or other adult asked to buy, give or pass on tobacco or a vape for someone under 18` THEN `the answer is` (`in the adult's words` (`Would an adult buying it for me offend` `the item` `the young person's age in years`))
    OTHERWISE `does not arise for you`
